meta {
  name: Complete Challenge
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/v1/auth/2fa/challenge
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "challenge_token": "{{challenge_token}}",
    "code": "123456"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.getStatus() === 200 && res.getBody().refresh_token) {
    bru.setEnvVar("refresh_token", res.getBody().refresh_token);
  }
}

docs {
  The second half of login for an account with 2FA. Unauthenticated by design: the
  `challenge_token` issued by `auth/Login (direct API)` *is* the credential, and the session
  it returns is the first thing the caller can actually use.

  Accepts a TOTP code or one of the recovery codes from enrolment. The challenge is one-shot,
  expires after five minutes, and is destroyed after five wrong codes. An accepted code cannot
  be replayed within its validity window.
}
